       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose looks like an error, and I'd like you to confirm it first.\n\n- **Ordered:** metformin 1700 mg PO three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum labeled dose:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, usually given as up to 850 mg three times daily. Extended-release is capped at 2,000\u20132,500 mg/day. Your order is about twice the maximum.\n- **Risk:** Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg/day total, for example 850 mg twice daily\n- 500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- Something else\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you want, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
